#%PAM-1.0
# Subarchy's lock screen, fingerprint (#93, ADR 0023). The lock runs this
# beside its password stack (subcult-lock), never in its place, and only
# when fprintd reports a finger enrolled for the user. Without fprintd or a
# reader the module fails and the password still unlocks. pam_fprintd's
# defaults hold: three touches or 30 seconds per check, then the lock
# starts another.
#
# pam_faillock (ADR 0063): an account locked by password failures is locked
# to the finger too, and a fingerprint unlock clears the failure count, as
# a password unlock does. Fingerprint misses are not counted, so a wrong
# finger cannot lock the password out. Each line is requisite or required
# and no other module can grant access, so only a matching finger unlocks.
# nodelay drops pam_faillock's 2-second wait after a failure, so a missing
# or broken reader fails at once and the lock backs off from it.
auth     requisite  pam_faillock.so preauth nodelay
auth     requisite  pam_fprintd.so
auth     required   pam_faillock.so authsucc
account  include    system-auth
